                <pb facs="0551" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg529"/>

                <head>No. 65.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to General Schenck.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 28,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>This Government declines to agree to the proposed altering of the supplementary
                    Article. The establishment of the principle embodied therein has been its object
                    in adhering to the presentation of the indirect claims, and its recognition is
                    the inducement for not pressing them before the Tribunal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
